<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	This file exists for exactly one key. Everything else in the app's Info.plist is
	still generated (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES) from INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings
	in the pbxproj — when INFOPLIST_FILE is also set, Xcode merges the generated keys on
	top of this file rather than replacing it, so this stays a one-key supplement.

	UIFileSharingEnabled has no INFOPLIST_KEY_ equivalent: Xcode only honours the fixed
	allowlist of INFOPLIST_KEY_* settings declared in its CoreBuildSystem.xcspec, and
	that key isn't in it (LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace is, which is why only half
	of the pair used to reach the built app — the app browsed documents in place but
	never appeared under "On My iPhone" in Files). An unrecognised INFOPLIST_KEY_ is
	dropped silently, with no build warning, so this needs to be a real plist entry.

	Both keys together are what exposes the app's Documents directory in Files.app.
	-->
	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
